cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Blitz or the Ares AI reasoning engine in academic research,
  technical whitepapers, security assessments, or publications, please
  cite this work using the metadata below. See LICENSE.md for the terms
  governing use of the software itself; citation of this work does not
  grant any rights under that license.
type: software
title: "Blitz: Automated IoT Red Teaming & Continuous Assessment Platform"
abstract: >-
  Blitz is a commercial, closed-loop automated red teaming and
  continuous assessment platform purpose-built for IoT and OT
  environments. It combines multi-protocol device discovery, an
  IoT-specific AI reasoning engine (Ares) for assessment planning, and
  a capability-gated authorization boundary (Ares Bridge) that enforces
  that only authorized actions reach real devices (see SECURITY.md,
  "Security Model — How Blitz Is Designed to Fail Safely"). Blitz runs
  a 12-stage closed-loop lifecycle spanning discovery, fingerprinting,
  planning, authorization, execution, evidence collection, findings
  generation, remediation, and automated re-validation. Ares is powered
  by a locally-run, fine-tuned Qwen3 (1.7B) model served via Ollama,
  keeping inference on-premises.
